# Secrets. .env holds live Meta/Bhashini/LLM tokens and an AES key; a COPY
# that pulls it in bakes them into an image layer, where they survive being
# "deleted" in a later layer and are readable by anyone who can pull it.
# Configuration reaches the container through the host's environment
# variables instead -- see render.yaml.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# 360MB of macOS-linked virtualenv. The image installs its own from
# requirements.txt; copying this in would both bloat the build context and
# shadow it with binaries compiled for the wrong platform.
.venv/
venv/

# The local demo database. Deployments use Postgres (DATABASE_URL).
*.db

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
tests/

.DS_Store
_to_delete/
